    "says": "",
    "means": "Total system cost divided by the number of tasks that satisfy a defined success criterion, including retries, failed runs, tool use, and evaluation overhead.",
    "whyItMatters": "A cheap model call can produce an expensive workflow if it fails often or requires repeated human correction.",
    "example": "Measure provider charges and infrastructure cost across 100 repository tasks, then divide by the number whose patches pass tests and review.",
    "confusion": "Cost per token measures usage. Cost per successful task measures useful outcomes.",
