    "term": "Least Privilege",
    "slug": "least-privilege",
    "letter": "L",
    "category": "Evaluation & safety",
    "says": "",
    "means": "Giving a model, agent, tool, or user only the permissions required for the current task, for only as long as those permissions are needed.",
    "whyItMatters": "Models can make mistakes or follow malicious instructions. Narrow permissions reduce the damage any one failure can cause.",
    "example": "Give a documentation agent read access to source files and write access to one branch, but no production credentials or merge permission.",
    "confusion": "Authentication proves identity. Least privilege limits what that identity can do.",
