    "whyItMatters": "Different modalities have different sampling rates, noise, spatial or temporal structure, and missing-data behavior, so one preprocessing assumption rarely fits all of them.",
    "example": "Document each modality's source, units, resolution, timing, preprocessing, and missing-value policy before designing alignment or fusion.",
    "confusion": "A modality is not merely a file extension or feature column. Several encodings can represent one modality, and one sample can contain several modalities.",
