    "letter": "R",
    "category": "Reliability & operations",
    "says": "",
    "means": "A bound on retry traffic, usually expressed relative to original requests or over a time window, that prevents retries from consuming unbounded capacity.",
    "whyItMatters": "When a dependency slows or fails, unrestricted retries multiply load exactly when the system has the least spare capacity.",
    "example": "Count retries separately from first attempts, cap them by service and tenant, honor deadlines, use jittered backoff, and stop retrying non-transient or non-idempotent failures.",
    "confusion": "A retry budget limits extra attempts. An error budget measures user-visible unreliability allowed by an SLO.",
    "aliases": [],
